# The speech recogniser is ~161 MB of ONNX graphs, fetched by
# scripts/fetch-stt-model.sh (pnpm models:fetch) rather than committed.
# Binaries this size are paid for by every clone and every bisect, forever.
*.onnx
tokens.txt
bpe.model

# Interrupted staging files. `fetch-stt-model.sh` moves each file into place
# atomically, so one of these means a run died mid-copy.
.*.part

# ATTRIBUTION.md is generated from catalogue.json beside every model the fetch
# script installs. The English model's copy is TRACKED so the licence notice is
# readable in a fresh clone, before anyone fetches or installs anything. It does
# NOT ship in the bundle — nothing under this directory does — and the installed
# copy is regenerated by `model_store::write_attribution`. The others are
# regenerated on fetch and would be untracked noise.
*/ATTRIBUTION.md
!x-asr-480ms/ATTRIBUTION.md

# The licence text copied beside the weights, for the same reason and on the
# same terms: the canonical copies are in legal/licenses/, and these are the
# ones a model directory needs to be complete on its own. Untracked — a second
# copy of an 11 KB legal text per model is noise in a diff, and the fetch
# script and `model_store::write_attribution` both write it.
*/LICENSE-*.txt
